     * billed unit (`pagesFetched`).
     *
     * @param string $id The artist, album, track or playlist: an open.spotify.com URL
     * (https://open.spotify.com/artist/06HL4z0CvFAxyc27GXpf02), a Spotify URI
     * (spotify:artist:06HL4z0CvFAxyc27GXpf02) or a bare 22-character id (then set `type`).
     * @param array{proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - proxy_country: Country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'DE', 'GB'). Spotify's
     * market follows it, which can change `playable` and search order; play counts are the same
     * everywhere. Leave blank for any.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /music/spotify.
     */
    public function spotifyTrack(string $id, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/music/spotify', [
            'type' => "track",
            'id' => $id,
            'proxy_country' => $options['proxy_country'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Scrape Spotify artists, albums, tracks, playlists and search.
     *
     * Returns Spotify catalog data as JSON, including the play counts and audience numbers the
     * official Web API does not expose. `type=artist`: `artist` (`followers`, `monthlyListeners`,
     * `worldRank`, `topCities`, `biography`, `externalLinks`, images, `verified`), `topTracks`
     * with `playcount` (a top track's `album` carries `name` and `releaseDate` when Spotify lists
     * that album among the artist's releases), `discography` groups (popular releases, albums,
     * singles, compilations with totals), `relatedArtists`, `appearsOn`, `featuredOn` /
     * `discoveredOn` playlists; `discography=true` adds the full `releases` list, paged.
     * `type=album`: `album` (type, release date, label, copyright, artists, cover) and `tracks`
     * with `playcount`, paged. `type=track`: `track` with `playcount`, duration, explicit flag,
     * album and every credited artist. `type=playlist`: `playlist` (name, description,
     * `followers`, owner, cover, `totalTracks`) and `tracks` with `playcount`, `addedAt`, `bpm`
     * and `key`, paged. `type=search&query=`: `results` of `search_type` tracks, artists, albums
     * or playlists, paged; a search with no match answers 200 with empty `results`. `playcount`
     * comes only on artist, album, track and playlist lookups: Spotify's search does not return
     * it, so search track results have no `playcount` key (look a track up with `type=track` for
     * its count). `id` takes an open.spotify.com URL, a Spotify URI or a bare id. Lists page with
     * `offset` / `max_results` and answer `hasMore` / `nextOffset`; each page fetched is one
     * billed unit (`pagesFetched`).
     *
     * @param string $id The artist, album, track or playlist: an open.spotify.com URL
     * (https://open.spotify.com/artist/06HL4z0CvFAxyc27GXpf02), a Spotify URI
     * (spotify:artist:06HL4z0CvFAxyc27GXpf02) or a bare 22-character id (then set `type`).
     * @param array{offset?: int, max_results?: int, proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - offset: 0-based position to start from in the list being paged: album tracks, playlist
     * tracks, search results, or the full discography with discography=true. Use the `nextOffset`
     * of a previous response to continue. Spotify serves search results up to position 1000. API
     * default: 0.
     *   - max_results: How many list items to collect. Album tracks: 1-1000 (default 100, 100 per
     * page). Playlist tracks: 1-2000 (default 100, 100 per page). Search: 1-1000 (default 20, 50
     * per page). Artist releases with discography=true: 1-1000 (default 50, 50 per page). Each
     * page fetched is one billed unit.
     *   - proxy_country: Country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'DE', 'GB'). Spotify's
     * market follows it, which can change `playable` and search order; play counts are the same
     * everywhere. Leave blank for any.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /music/spotify.
     */
    public function spotifyPlaylist(string $id, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/music/spotify', [
            'type' => "playlist",
            'id' => $id,
            'offset' => $options['offset'] ?? null,
            'max_results' => $options['max_results'] ?? null,
            'proxy_country' => $options['proxy_country'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Scrape a public Telegram channel: info and posts.
     *
     * Reads a public Telegram channel's web preview. Returns `channel` (`username`, `title`,
     * `description`, `avatar`, `verified`, `subscribers` and the other `counters`) and `posts`,
     * newest first: `id`, `url`, `date` (ISO-8601 UTC), `text` (plain), `textHtml`, `views`,
     * `author` (signature), `edited`, `forwardedFrom`, `replyTo`, `media` (photo / video /
     * animation / round_video / voice / audio / document / sticker, with CDN `url`, `thumbnail`,
     * `duration`), `poll`, `linkPreview`, `reactions` (a custom-emoji reaction has its
     * `customEmojiId`, plus the standard `emoji` and `image` Telegram falls back to when the page
     * shows that emoji anywhere), `buttons`, `links`, `hashtags` (the tags Telegram links; a bare
     * '#7' is text) and `mentions`. One page (about 20 posts) by default; `max_posts` (up to 500)
     * pages back through history; `before`, `after` and `since` bound the range, `q` searches
     * inside the channel and `post_id` returns one post. `nextBefore` continues a capped answer.
     * Only channels have a public preview: users, bots, groups and private channels answer 404.
     * Billed one request per page fetched (`pagesFetched`).
     *
     * @param string $channel Public channel: username ('durov'), '@durov', or a t.me link
     * ('https://t.me/durov', 'https://t.me/s/durov'). A post link ('https://t.me/durov/400')
     * returns that one post.
     * @param array{max_posts?: int, before?: int, after?: int, since?: string, q?: string, post_id?: int, proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - max_posts: Posts to collect, newest first (1-500), paging back through the channel's
     * history; each page fetched is billed as one request. Omit it for one page, billed once: the
     * newest posts (a page has 20 message slots and an album fills one per photo, so it can hold
     * fewer posts).
     *   - before: Only posts with an id below this one. Pass `nextBefore` of a previous response
     * to continue where it stopped.
     *   - after: Stop at this post id: only posts with a higher id are returned.
     *   - since: Stop at this date: only posts published on or after it (YYYY-MM-DD or an ISO-8601
     * datetime, UTC when no offset is given).
     *   - q: Search inside the channel: only posts matching this text.
     *   - post_id: Return only this post (a post id of the channel).
     *   - proxy_country: Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US', 'DE'). Leave
     * blank to let the API pick.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /social/telegram-channel.
     */
    public function telegramChannel(string $channel, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/social/telegram-channel', [
            'channel' => $channel,
            'max_posts' => $options['max_posts'] ?? null,
            'before' => $options['before'] ?? null,
            'after' => $options['after'] ?? null,
            'since' => $options['since'] ?? null,
            'q' => $options['q'] ?? null,
            'post_id' => $options['post_id'] ?? null,
            'proxy_country' => $options['proxy_country'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Scrape Quora questions, answers and profiles.
     *
     * Given a Quora `question` (URL or slug), returns the `question` (`qid`, `title`, `url`,
     * `answerCount`, `allRelatedCount`, `followerCount`, `commentCount`, `topics`) and its
     * `answers`: `id`, `url`, `relation` (`answer`, `merged` for an answer to a question Quora
     * merged into this one, `related` with `include_related=true`), the answered `question`,
     * `author` (`name`, `uid`, `profileUrl`, `imageUrl`, `credential`, `isVerified`,
     * `isAnonymous`), the full `text` with `images` and `links`, `upvotes`, `views`, `shares`,
     * `comments`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `isAiGenerated`; plus `relatedQuestions`. Answers
     * are in Quora's own order, up to `max_answers` (10 per page after the first few), unique
     * within a call. `nextCursor` as `cursor` continues, best-effort: Quora re-ranks the list on
     * every visit, so a continuation can repeat or skip answers of earlier calls (dedupe by `id`);
     * for a complete list ask for a larger `max_answers` in one call (up to 300).
     * `mode=profile&profile=` returns a public `profile` (`name`, `headline`, `description`,
     * follower / following / answer / question / post counts, `contentViews`, `credentials`,
     * `knowsAbout`, `spaces`, `topWriterYears`, `joinedAt`) with its newest `answers`. No login:
     * only what Quora shows an anonymous visitor - Quora's search is not available that way, and
     * Quora lists only a profile's newest few dozen answers to logged-out visitors
     * (`pagingStopped`: `quora_logged_out_limit`). `pagingStopped` otherwise names why paging
     * ended early (`blocked`, `time`, `unavailable`). Billed one unit per page fetched
     * (`pagesFetched`); a `cursor` continuation bills only its GraphQL pages.
     *
     * @param string $question Quora question URL (https://www.quora.com/What-is-the-best-way-to-
     * learn-programming), an answer URL on it, or the question slug (What-is-the-best-way-to-
     * learn-programming). Language editions such as es.quora.com are accepted as URLs. Required
     * with mode=question.
     * @param array{max_answers?: int, include_related?: bool, cursor?: string, proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - max_answers: Answers to return: 1-300 with mode=question (default 20), 0-200 with
     * mode=profile (default 10; 0 = profile only). Answers come 10 per page after the first few;
     * each page is one billed unit.
     *   - include_related: mode=question: also return the answers Quora shows from related
     * questions (its 'All related' view, `relation`='related'). By default only answers to this
     * question and to questions merged into it. API default: false.
     *   - cursor: Continue after a previous call: pass its `nextCursor`. Best-effort: each call is
     * a new Quora visit and Quora re-ranks the list per visit, so a continuation can repeat or
     * skip answers of earlier calls - dedupe by answer `id`. For a complete list ask for a larger
     * `max_answers` in one call (up to 300).
     *   - proxy_country: Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US', 'DE'). Leave
     * blank for the countries chosen for the site.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /social/quora.
     */
    public function quoraQuestion(string $question, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/social/quora', [
            'mode' => "question",
            'question' => $question,
            'max_answers' => $options['max_answers'] ?? null,
            'include_related' => $options['include_related'] ?? null,
            'cursor' => $options['cursor'] ?? null,
            'proxy_country' => $options['proxy_country'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Scrape Quora questions, answers and profiles.
     *
     * Given a Quora `question` (URL or slug), returns the `question` (`qid`, `title`, `url`,
     * `answerCount`, `allRelatedCount`, `followerCount`, `commentCount`, `topics`) and its
     * `answers`: `id`, `url`, `relation` (`answer`, `merged` for an answer to a question Quora
     * merged into this one, `related` with `include_related=true`), the answered `question`,
     * `author` (`name`, `uid`, `profileUrl`, `imageUrl`, `credential`, `isVerified`,
     * `isAnonymous`), the full `text` with `images` and `links`, `upvotes`, `views`, `shares`,
     * `comments`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `isAiGenerated`; plus `relatedQuestions`. Answers
     * are in Quora's own order, up to `max_answers` (10 per page after the first few), unique
     * within a call. `nextCursor` as `cursor` continues, best-effort: Quora re-ranks the list on
     * every visit, so a continuation can repeat or skip answers of earlier calls (dedupe by `id`);
     * for a complete list ask for a larger `max_answers` in one call (up to 300).
     * `mode=profile&profile=` returns a public `profile` (`name`, `headline`, `description`,
     * follower / following / answer / question / post counts, `contentViews`, `credentials`,
     * `knowsAbout`, `spaces`, `topWriterYears`, `joinedAt`) with its newest `answers`. No login:
     * only what Quora shows an anonymous visitor - Quora's search is not available that way, and
     * Quora lists only a profile's newest few dozen answers to logged-out visitors
     * (`pagingStopped`: `quora_logged_out_limit`). `pagingStopped` otherwise names why paging
     * ended early (`blocked`, `time`, `unavailable`). Billed one unit per page fetched
     * (`pagesFetched`); a `cursor` continuation bills only its GraphQL pages.
     *
     * @param string $profile Quora profile URL (https://www.quora.com/profile/Adam-DAngelo) or
     * profile slug (Adam-DAngelo). Required with mode=profile.
     * @param array{max_answers?: int, cursor?: string, proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - max_answers: Answers to return: 1-300 with mode=question (default 20), 0-200 with
     * mode=profile (default 10; 0 = profile only). Answers come 10 per page after the first few;
     * each page is one billed unit.
     *   - cursor: Continue after a previous call: pass its `nextCursor`. Best-effort: each call is
     * a new Quora visit and Quora re-ranks the list per visit, so a continuation can repeat or
     * skip answers of earlier calls - dedupe by answer `id`. For a complete list ask for a larger
     * `max_answers` in one call (up to 300).
     *   - proxy_country: Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US', 'DE'). Leave
     * blank for the countries chosen for the site.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /social/quora.
     */
    public function quoraProfile(string $profile, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/social/quora', [
            'mode' => "profile",
            'profile' => $profile,
            'max_answers' => $options['max_answers'] ?? null,
            'cursor' => $options['cursor'] ?? null,
            'proxy_country' => $options['proxy_country'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Get a website's Similarweb traffic overview.
     *
     * Returns Similarweb's public traffic overview for `domain` as JSON: `globalRank`,
     * `countryRank` (with `country`), `categoryRank` (with `category`) and their month-over-month
     * changes; `totalVisits` for the latest month with `visitsChangePercent`; `bounceRate`,
     * `pagesPerVisit`, `avgVisitDuration`/`avgVisitDurationSeconds`; `visitsHistory` (the last 3
     * months - earlier months are derived from Similarweb's own month-over-month change) and
     * `rankHistory`; `trafficSources` (channel shares - Similarweb's free page reveals only some,
     * the rest are null); `topCountries`; `demographics` (gender, age groups); `competitors`
     * (similar sites with affinity); `search` (organic/paid split and top keywords);
     * `socialNetworks`, `referrals`, `outgoingLinks`, `displayAds`; `technologies`;
     * `audienceInterests`; and the `company` profile. `snapshotDate` is the month the data
     * describes. A domain Similarweb has no page for returns `found: false` with the same keys set
     * to null/empty; a known domain too small to estimate returns `hasTrafficData: false`.
     *
     * @param string $domain Website to look up: a bare domain ('github.com'), a URL
     * ('https://www.github.com/about'), or a Similarweb page URL. A leading 'www.' is dropped;
     * other subdomains ('docs.python.org') are kept.
     * @param array{proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - proxy_country: Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US', 'DE').
     * Optional.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /seo/similarweb.
     */
    public function similarwebOverview(string $domain, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/seo/similarweb', [
            'domain' => $domain,
            'proxy_country' => $options['proxy_country'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Run Ahrefs' free SEO tools (DR, backlinks, traffic, keywords, KD, SERP).
     *
     * Ahrefs' free SEO tools as JSON, without an Ahrefs account. `tool=authority&target=<domain>`:
     * `domainRating`, `backlinks`, `referringDomains`, `dofollowBacklinksPercent`,
     * `dofollowReferringDomainsPercent`. `tool=backlinks`: the same plus `topBacklinks`
     * (`urlFrom`, `urlTo`, `title`, `anchor`, `textBefore`/`textAfter`, `domainRating`).
     * `tool=traffic`: `organicTraffic`, `trafficValueUsd`, `trafficHistory`, `topPages`,
     * `topCountries`, `topKeywords` (`country` narrows it to one market). `tool=broken-links`:
     * `inbound` broken backlinks and `outbound` broken links on the site's pages. `tool=keyword-
     * difficulty&keyword=<phrase>`: `difficulty` (0-100), `referringDomainsToRank` and the SERP
     * `results`. `tool=keywords`: `ideas` and `questionIdeas` with `difficulty` and `volume`
     * buckets, plus totals (Google). `tool=serp`: the top Google `results` (organic with `metrics`
     * - DR, UR, backlinks, referring domains, traffic, value, keywords - plus AI overview,
     * questions, shopping, local and news blocks). Domain tools take `mode` (subdomains, domain,
     * prefix, exact). One call, one unit.
     *
     * @param string $tool Which Ahrefs free tool to run: 'authority' (Domain Rating), 'backlinks',
     * 'traffic', 'broken-links' (these take `target`), 'keyword-difficulty', 'keywords' (keyword
     * ideas), 'serp' (these take `keyword`).
     * @param array{target?: string, keyword?: string, country?: string, mode?: string, protocol?: string, questions?: bool} $options
     *   - target: Domain or URL for the domain tools, e.g. 'github.com' or
     * 'https://github.com/features'.
     *   - keyword: Search phrase for the keyword tools, e.g. 'running shoes'.
     *   - country: Two-letter market code. Keyword tools: the search market (default 'us').
     * traffic: limits the estimate to that country (default: worldwide). Not used by the other
     * domain tools.
     *   - mode: Target scope for the domain tools: 'subdomains' (the domain with all its
     * subdomains), 'domain' (without subdomains), 'prefix' (everything under the URL) or 'exact'
     * (that URL only). API default: subdomains.
     *   - protocol: traffic only: 'both', 'http' or 'https'. API default: both.
     *   - questions: keywords only: also return question ideas. API default: true.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /seo/ahrefs.
     */
    public function ahrefs(string $tool, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/seo/ahrefs', [
            'tool' => $tool,
            'target' => $options['target'] ?? null,
            'keyword' => $options['keyword'] ?? null,
            'country' => $options['country'] ?? null,
            'mode' => $options['mode'] ?? null,
            'protocol' => $options['protocol'] ?? null,
            'questions' => $options['questions'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Get a website's Semrush overview (Authority Score, traffic, backlinks).
     *
     * Semrush's public website data for `domain`, without a Semrush account. `report=overview`
     * (default): `authorityScore`, `globalRank`, `countryRank`, `categoryRank`, `visits` with
     * `visitsChangePercent` and `visitsHistory` (desktop/mobile), `pagesPerVisit`,
     * `timeOnSiteSeconds`, `bounceRate`, `searchTraffic` (organic and paid with history),
     * `backlinks` (backlinks, referring domains, Google penalty risk, history), `topKeywords`
     * (position, search volume, CPC, traffic share, intent), `topCountries`, `competitors`,
     * `trafficSources` (incoming and outgoing) and `aiTraffic` (visits from AI assistants).
     * `report=competitors`: the domain's competitors, each with Authority Score, ranks, visits and
     * engagement. Semrush publishes these pages for about 200k of the most visited sites; any
     * other domain returns `found: false`. One call, one unit.
     *
     * @param string $domain Website to look up: a domain ('github.com'), a URL
     * ('https://www.github.com/about') or a Semrush website page URL. A leading 'www.' is dropped;
     * other subdomains are kept.
     * @param array{report?: string} $options
     *   - report: 'overview' (traffic, rank, search traffic, backlinks, keywords, countries,
     * competitors, sources) or 'competitors' (the competitor list with each one's ranks, visits
     * and engagement). API default: overview.
     * @return array<mixed>
     * Calls POST /seo/semrush.
     */
    public function semrushOverview(string $domain, array $options = []): array
    {
        return $this->postJson('/seo/semrush', [
            'domain' => $domain,
            'report' => $options['report'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /** @param string|string[]|null $value */
    private static function pluginJoin($value, string $sep): ?string
    {
        return is_array($value) ? implode($sep, $value) : $value;
    }
}
